# `ds_engine_mem`'s counts ([NDBG.2.1]): `13_negation_over_derived`'s steps
# with a `mem` read before anything and after the pump. The fixture has two
# rules: `make_artifact` (a root beta over Build, and a NOT
# node over Refusal below it) and `publish_refusal` (a root beta over
# RefusalText). So the read at the start is the empty network -- the nodes, a
# nil token in each root's left memory, no facts -- and the read after the pump
# counts the facts, the alpha memories and the NOT node's left memory after
# the Refusal blocked the Build token.
#
# Each `mem` line compares wm_fact_count (synthetic facts included), the node
# counts, alpha_match_count and beta_token_count (every beta's left memory):
# the counts [NDBG.2.1] says two runtimes report alike. The byte and intern
# fields are implementation-defined ([NDBG.2.1], [NMET.4.7]).
# @spec [NDBG.2.1]
mem
assert Build id=1
assert RefusalText id=1
pump
mem
